nt she would add another gold, making her four-for-four. Her time of 59.00 was the second fastest ever in the event, but over a full second behind Meagher’s world record. Meagher was not a factor, placing seventh in the final. She would manage a bronze in the 200 butterfly two days later in Seoul and then retire after the 1988 Olympics. Silver in the event went to Otto’s teammate " [:a {:href "/athletes/47555"} "Birte Weigang"] ", who would also win silver in the 200 fly in 1988. The bronze medalist, " [:a {:href "/athletes/46100"} "Qian Hong"] " of China, would return in four years and win the gold medal in Barcelona."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Otto would end the Seoul Olympics with six gold medals in six events, a record for women in the Olympics in any sport. She is the only swimmer to win golds in three different strokes at the Olympic Games."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "B Final"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "177"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/47512"} "Kristin Otto"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GDR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GDR.png"}] "GDR"]] [:td {} "1:00.40 (1 h5)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "59.00 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "183"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/47555"} "Birte Weigang"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GDR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GDR.png"}] "GDR"]] [:td {} "59.97 (2 h6)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "59.45 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "79"] [:td {} [:a {:href 